// Sends main's plugin approval cards back to where the request was made (mode "session"), instead
// of every card to Adam's Telegram chat (mode "targets", Adam's yes of 2026-11-10).
// Adam, 2026-11-22: "make it so that the hud requests don't go to telegram". By OpenClaw
// 2026.10.9's source (resolveForwardTargets, resolveSessionDeliveryTarget):
// - typed in the Mac HUD or the Control UI ("webchat"): no chat to forward to, so the card shows
//   only on the Gateway's approval clients: the HUD that asked, and admin clients (the iOS app);
// - Telegram: the card goes to that Telegram chat;
// - voice ("voice" is not a deliverable channel): falls back to the session's last chat, Telegram,
//   until ADR 0010's voice confirmation is built. Checked live after the switch.
// targets stays filled, so the undo is mode "targets" alone. It is ignored in mode "session".
// TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID is filled in on the PC from channels.telegram.allowFrom by
// scripts/pc/apply-approvals.sh, so the chat ID never enters this public repo.
// Undo: mode "targets" (every card to Telegram again), or approvals.plugin.enabled false.
{
  approvals: {
    plugin: {
      enabled: true,
      mode: "session",
      agentFilter: ["main"],
      targets: [{ channel: "telegram", to: "TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID" }],
    },
  },
}
